<title>USA: N.Y. Senate moves to slash state business taxes.</title>
<headline>N.Y. Senate moves to slash state business taxes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Senate on Tuesday launched an ambitious plan to slash business taxes by nearly $2.5 billion over five years.</p>
<p>&quot;To those who say we cannot afford more tax cuts, I say we cannot afford not to cut taxes,&quot; said Joseph Bruno, R-Troy, in prepared remarks.</p>
<p>Bruno, the Senate majority leader, said the Senate was again taking the lead, as it had in the past three years, when state taxes were cut by about $6.0 billion.</p>
</text>
